# Clean Code, SOLID, DRY

- Write clear names, small functions, and obvious control flow.
- Apply SOLID: single responsibility, depend on abstractions (ports), keep modules open for extension.
- Apply DRY: extract shared logic once; do not copy-paste across layers or contexts.
- Soft limit ~300 lines per file. Split by responsibility before a file grows large.
- No god classes, no mega route files, no catch-all utility dumps.
- Prefer explicit errors over silent failures.
